---
import ReferenceTable from '../../components/ReferenceTable.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.governance;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">Stewardship and public process</p>
    <h2>Current stewardship</h2>
    <p>TENSOR operates under the TENSOR Standards Consortium project identity. On October 11, 2026, John Schieferle Uhlenbrock accepted bootstrap stewardship and the operational roles below.</p>
    <ReferenceTable label="Stewardship roles"><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Current holder</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Convenor</td><td>Review coordination, scope, decisions, and escalation.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr><tr><td>Core editor</td><td>Specification text and consistent semantics.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr><tr><td>Conformance maintainer</td><td>Fixtures, check coverage, and implementation evidence.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr><tr><td>Profile editors</td><td>Domain definitions and source quality.</td><td>Unassigned</td></tr><tr><td>Independent reviewers</td><td>Practitioner, research, and implementation review.</td><td>Open participation</td></tr></tbody></ReferenceTable>
    <p>These operational roles currently rest with one founder. The <a href="/read/docs/stewardship/">stewardship record</a> lists disclosure and infrastructure-continuity items that remain pending.</p>
    <h2>Governance proposal</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/read/founding/02-governance/">governance proposal</a> defines public review, conflict disclosure, decision records, appeals, and a possible transition to broader stewardship. It remains unadopted; a council, independent appeal body, and separate legal entity are not established by that proposal.</p>
    <p>The proposed public foundation includes the specification, essential profiles, schemas, and basic conformance materials. Vendor and organization participation is part of the model. Funding and sponsorship do not determine shared investigative meaning.</p>
    <h2>Proposed decision process</h2>
    <ol><li>A numbered proposal records the problem, examples, alternatives, compatibility effects, and acceptance evidence.</li><li>Review lasts at least 14 days for technical changes and 30 days for breaking, charter, or governance changes.</li><li>Substantive objections and their disposition remain in the public record. Material revisions restart review.</li><li>The decision record names the rationale, reviewers, conflicts, and unresolved issues.</li><li>Approved text, schemas, fixtures, and migration guidance are archived together.</li></ol>
    <p>The proposed stable-release gate includes substantive assessments from at least two reviewers independent of the principal authors and each other.</p>
    <h2>Findings and proposals</h2>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=implementation-report.yml">Technical findings and implementation reports</a> and <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=core-rfc.yml">change proposals</a> use the Framework repository. The convenor coordinates the <a href="/read/docs/review-process/">finding, dissent, and escalation process</a>. Sensitive vulnerabilities use <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/security/advisories/new">private reporting</a>.</p>
    <h2>Rights and participation</h2>
    <p>Existing materials retain their published licenses. Proposed contribution, patent, and stewardship policies require explicit review before adoption. Public contributions include source attribution, relevant affiliations, and conflict disclosures. Case material is illustrative or authorized for disclosure.</p>
    <p><a href="/contribute/">Contribution guide</a> · <a href="/read/founding/00-charter/">Founding charter</a> · <a href="/review/">Technical review</a></p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
